# Frontend

- Stack: React, TypeScript, and Vite. Styles live in `src/index.css`. There is no Tailwind and no React Router.
- `src/routes/` is the address bar. `src/library/` is the saved-song list. `src/lyrics/` is the four documents. `src/player/` is the player and the MP3 form. `src/new-song.tsx` is the Groq chat for a new song.
- Component-local state. No global state package.
- The documents are Original, Hiragana, Romaji, and English, in that order.
- Japanese text gets `lang="ja"`. Render lyric text as plain React text, never as HTML.
- Layer visibility lives in `sessionStorage`. Any layer can be hidden, including the last one. Invalid stored values fall back to all visible.
- The player has only the approved controls. Playback does not highlight or scroll the lyrics. On a wide window, hover or focus marks the same line across the open documents.
- Accessibility: semantic landmarks, headings, and lists; labelled controls with pressed, muted, and value state; visible focus; reduced motion respected; never rely on color alone.
- Every async boundary has loading, success or empty, recoverable error with retry, and unknown error states.
- `src/contracts.ts` mirrors `backend/app/contracts.py`; change both together.
- Run frontend commands from `frontend/`.
